               WITNESS IDENTIFICATION AND QUALIFICATIONS

Q.   Please state your name and business address.

A.   My name is Zoë E. Lees. My business address is 119 E. Marcy St. Suite 202, Santa Fe,

     New Mexico 87501.

Q.   On whose behalf are you testifying in this proceeding?

A.   I am filing testimony on behalf of Southwestern Public Service Company, a New Mexico

     corporation (“SPS”) and wholly-owned electric utility subsidiary of Xcel Energy Inc.

     (“Xcel Energy”).

Q.   By whom are you employed and in what position?

A.   I am employed by SPS as Regional Vice President (“RVP”), Regulatory Planning and

     Policy.

Q.   Please outline your responsibilities as RVP, Regulatory Planning and Policy.

A.   As RVP, Regulatory Planning and Policy, I direct SPS’s regulatory strategy, filings, and

     compliance activities across all jurisdictions. I oversee regulatory staff responsible for

     ratemaking and revenue recovery, planning, policy development, and resource acquisition.

     I direct the development of all such regulatory case filings in coordination with subject

     matter experts and legal counsel. I also oversee SPS’s participation in many Public Utility

     Commission of Texas (“PUCT”) and New Mexico Public Regulation Commission

     (“Commission”) rulemakings, including some matters with the Federal Energy Regulatory

     Commission.




                                              1
                                        EXHIBIT A


Q.   Please describe your educational background.

A.   I hold a Juris Doctor from the University of New Mexico School of Law and a Bachelor of

     Arts from Wheaton College in Massachusetts. I was also named a Fulbright Scholar to the

     Institute of International Education, Malaysia, in 2006, completing my term in country in

     2007.

Q.   Please describe your professional experience.

A.   I have worked for Xcel Energy since 2019. I started in March 2019 as a Principal Attorney

     representing SPS at the Commission in regulatory proceedings and in rulemakings. I was

     promoted to my current position with SPS as RVP, Regulatory Planning and Policy, in

     March 2023. Before joining Xcel Energy, I privately practiced law in New Mexico from

     2013 to 2019. My practice there focused on utility regulation, natural resources law, and

     litigation.

Q.   Have you testified or filed testimony before any regulatory authorities?

A.   Yes. I filed testimony before the Commission in Case Nos. 23-00071-UT, 23-00230-UT,

     23-00271-UT, 24-00240-UT, and 25-00066-UT, as well as in Docket No. 58664 before the

     Public Utility Commission of Texas.




